# Code-quality rules

- Do not use `any` unless unavoidable and documented.
- Validate external API responses with Zod.
- Keep controllers thin; put business logic in services.
- Put Riot-specific logic behind a provider interface.
- Use dependency injection.
- Add typed error classes and structured logging.
- Do not swallow exceptions or expose stack traces to users.
- Use UTC timestamps in storage.
- Add database indexes for frequently queried fields.
- Make ingestion jobs idempotent; do not duplicate completed matches.
- Avoid large components and large service files.
- Add comments only where behavior is not self-explanatory.
